# CentCompras core

## Project

Central warehouse + satellite branches. Django 6.1, PostgreSQL, plain HTML/JS. Phases 0–4 are done: catalogue + pricing + purchase orders + goods receipt + manager catalog. Branches, orders, offline, and email are later (deferred/pending).

## What exists today

- `accounts` — custom User (email, timezone), warehouse groups, login
- `products` — catalogue + selling prices + `SupplierItemPrice`, staff console `/manage/items/`, manager catalog `/manage/catalog/` (read-only stock + prices)
- `procurement` — purchase orders at `/manage/purchase-orders/`
- `inventory` — goods receipt + `StockMovement` ledger + cached `Item.quantity` at `/manage/goods-receipts/`
- `logging_utils` — rotating logs in `logs/`
- `branches` — **not built** (design in `docs/warehouse-tenancy-setup.md`)
- `orders` — not built; wait until Phase 5
- Offline catalogue — **removed** (Phase 7 may re-add it)

## Non-negotiables

- PostgreSQL = source of truth. No client-side writes.
- Business logic in `services.py`; views/commands stay thin
- Warehouse groups (`warehouse_admins`, `warehouse_managers`, `warehouse_data_operators`); `/admin/` is superuser only
- Plain Django + plain JavaScript — no React/Vue
- Incremental phases — no large application dumps
- Do not implement the tenancy-doc `Order` stub (`item_name`)
- Do not start branches, orders, offline, email, or shared chrome in passing
- Do not restyle `/` or polish the staff console unless that session is requested

